{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,76p;108,255p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,76p;108,255p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Linking related questions: the build design, version 5 (D694, D695; for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D694) and narrowed the first version (D695, \"只连数字题\"): a link joins a **newly opened number question** and an **open\n     4\tnumber question it was shown**, in either reading direction; both are asset questions with five-rung ladders and typed bounds. No\n     5\ttheme, event or same-article pair is linked in this version. A chosen link leaves filing alone (D694 (a)). Version 1 of this document\n     6\twas reviewed in council R round 4 (`codex-r4.md`, NOT READY), version 2 in round 5 (`codex-r5.md`, NOT READY), version 3 in round 6\n     7\t(`codex-r6.md`, NOT READY), version 4 in round 7 (`codex-r7.md`, NOT READY); each finding is answered below (§10).\n     8\t\n     9\t## 0. Versions and entry points\n    10\t\n    11\t- `poc/config/poc-v119.json`: poc-v118 with `matching.engine` `jev-links` and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`; nothing else.\n    12\t- `judging-v8.txt` is a byte copy of `judging-v7.txt`; only the code-built dependency block differs (§3). A request with no dependency is\n    13\t  byte-equal under v7 and v8.\n    14\t- `config.ENGINES` gains `jev-links`. Every place that tests `engine == 'jev'` (`round._match`, `scripts/replay.py`,\n    15\t  `parallel_day.ParallelDay`, `budget_replay.py` defaults) treats `jev-links` as Jev; only `round.run` asks the link questions, and only\n    16\t  under `jev-links`. Existing Jev requests are unchanged (`jev.request_for` holds model, state and questions only).\n    17\t- **Who may run poc-v119 (an enforced boundary):** only the July harness (`TEST-PLAN.md`). `scripts/replay.py` and\n    18\t  `budget_replay.py` refuse a configuration whose matching engine is `jev-links` (\"not a product entry point in this version\"). The\n    19\t  harness holds `live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the whole run, refuses a store whose last day is unfinished, and never\n    20\t  resumes a sequence that stopped: a stopped sequence is final and reported as stopped. Each harness ledger is **marked harness-only**\n    21\t  before the run (a table `harness_only` holding the harness's name and the date), and both ordinary writers refuse it under any\n    22\t  configuration before routing an item (`scripts/replay.py`'s `refuse_harness_ledger`, called beside `refuse_seeded_ledger`, which\n    23\t  `budget_replay.py` already calls); read-only inspection stays open. So the serial path's unchecked restarts (a\n    24\t  sequence reused under another configuration or input, a second writer) cannot reach a v119 store. Making poc-v119 runnable from the\n    25\t  product entry point is a later decision, with its own restart rules.\n    26\t- **A store written by poc-v119 opened by poc-v118:** allowed; v118 writes no link, renders a stored link with today's v7 line, and\n    27\t  filing skips it (filing reads the stored kind, not the configuration). A run is meant to keep one configuration; this is the defined\n    28\t  outcome if it does not.\n    29\t- Pins (`tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py`): the v7 pins stay; added: `judging-v8.txt`'s sha (equal to v7's), the two new\n    30\t  question builders' output, judging-v8's schema (equal to v7's), and a request-level control: one ledger with a link rendered under v8\n    31\t  (exact text) and under v7 (today's text), and one without a link, byte-equal under both.\n    32\t\n    33\t## 1. Where selection runs: after matching has settled what opens\n    34\t\n    35\tIn `round.run`, under `jev-links` only, a new step **after the evidence-only second matching call returns and before the `matched`\n    36\tsuccess marker**, on the first call's `checked.outcomes` and lists:\n    37\t1. From `checked.outcomes` take the candidates whose outcome is `new` or `succession`; `identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates,\n    38\t   checked.outcomes)` gives their aliases; one canonical candidate per stored question. A candidate refused or not opened is not asked.\n    39\t2. **Eligible pairs:** the canonical candidate C and each open thesis T on C's list (its search list plus the item's shown questions,\n    40\t   `lists.candidate_lists[C] + shown`, the list its relation questions used), when both are **number questions**: asset kind; a\n    41\t   measure outside `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (C's own key, T's stored key); five rungs whose canonical labels run Strongly bullish to\n    42\t   Strongly bearish or the reverse; a **typed direction** (§5). C's rungs are taken as the writer will store them\n    43\t   (`writing.oriented_like` for a succession, which may reverse the whole ladder with its labels). A pair outside this set is not\n    44\t   asked. Same-article pairs are not asked (D695).\n    45\t3. **Stage 1, one Jev job per C:** state = `candidate_state(C)`; per eligible T the `READS` question (§2) with `thesis_text(T)`.\n    46\t4. **Stage 2, one Jev job per C with a passing stage-1 answer:** the shared state stays `candidate_state(C)`; per such pair one of two\n    47\t   sign questions, chosen by the stage-1 direction, each naming in its own instructions which question reads which (§2). One job can\n    48\t   hold both directions.\n    49\t5. **The graph check** (§4) on the whole proposed set of the article (every opening candidate's links) plus the stored reading\n    50\t   relation; candidates are represented by their canonical ids until written.\n    51\t6. The selection is recorded in a **new append-only table `link_selections`** (id, attempt_id, seq, input_id, config checksum, status,\n    52\t   record_json). It is not a `match_records` row, so preflight and the trace grouping (which read `call_no`) are untouched; its readers\n    53\t   are the July test and the tests that pin its shape. Per attempt (`attempt_id` = the article's input id and a counter):\n    54\t   - **`proposed`**, inserted before the write savepoint, so a failed write does not roll it back (round.run's failure path commits\n    55\t     the open transaction): every pair shown with its eligibility, each Jev call's call id and request sha, every answer's choice and\n    56\t     probabilities, each correction with the rejected direction and its path, the links proposed with direction and sign;\n    57\t   - **`committed`**, in the article's own commit: the rows written, each with its final label;\n    58\t   - **`failed`**, after the rollback, in the transaction `round._fail` commits (alone, with the partial answers, when a Jev call fails\n    59\t     before any proposal exists): the reason (persistent circle, write conflict, the\n    60\t     waiting-row refusal) or, when `jev.ask` raised, the error and the computed request sha of the failing request (from\n    61\t     `jev.request_for` and `model.request_identity`; a transport failure may leave no archive row), with what had been answered\n    62\t     before it.\n    63\t7. `writing.write` gains a keyword-only argument `proposed_links=None` (today's six-argument callers unchanged), carrying the canonical\n    64\t   endpoints, direction and sign; the write resolves C's new id, computes the label from the stored rungs and writes (§4).\n    65\t\n    66\t`jev.ask` failures (transport or answer shape) fail the article at the step `matched` as a matching failure does today: resumable, and\n    67\ta resume re-asks only what the archive lacks.\n    68\t\n    69\t## 2. The two questions\n    70\t\n    71\t```\n    72\tREADS (choice), state = CANDIDATE (candidate_state), per THESIS:\n    73\t instructions: \"Should one of these two questions be judged with the other's current conclusion in view? Use only the supplied text. THESIS:\\n\" + thesis_text(T)\n    74\t \"candidate_reads_thesis\": \"the CANDIDATE should be judged with the THESIS's current conclusion in view, because the THESIS's answer bounds or drives the CANDIDATE's: a part read against its whole (one product line's sales against the company's total sales; one region's loan book against the bank's total loans), or a quantity read against another it depends on (a component supplier's revenue against its largest customer's capital spending; an airline's fuel bill against its fuel volume)\"\n    75\t \"thesis_reads_candidate\": \"the THESIS should be judged with the CANDIDATE's current conclusion in view, for the same reasons with the roles swapped\"\n    76\t \"neither\": \"neither answer bounds or drives the other: unrelated quantities (a retailer's gross margin and its store openings in another country), or the same quantity for the same period and scope; sharing a company, industry or topic is not enough\"\n   108\t`changed` unchanged, reaches the reader at the reader's next judgement, not in the same round (the round queues on `changed`, as for\n   109\tevery dependency today).\n   110\t\n   111\t## 4. The graph, the circle correction and the writer\n   112\t\n   113\t- **Graph check (one owner, `links.check_graph`, run at selection and again inside the write savepoint):** the reading relation =\n   114\t  every stored dependency row (all kinds) read at its **effective target** (`store.dependencies_of`'s `resolved_to`: a bound legacy\n   115\t  wait counts through the question it is bound to) plus **every proposed link of the article**, the canonical candidates as nodes. Any circle\n   116\t  in that whole graph is found, including one through two openings and no stored path (C1 → T1 → C2 → T2 → C1).\n   117\t- **Waiting rows (admission):** under `jev-links` the link step refuses a store holding an unbound waiting row (a `dependencies` row\n   118\t  with a waited year and no target), failing the article at `matched` with that reason; so no waiting row can bind in the same write\n   119\t  and close a circle unseen. Product stores hold none (the three poc-v118 draws: 0 dependency rows); a test exercises the refusal.\n   120\t- **Correction (PRD 06: \"Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling\"):** for each\n   121\t  proposed link on a circle, one correction request: the stage-1 question for that pair again, its instructions extended with \"Reading\n   122\t  this way would make <R> read itself through <path>; a question cannot read its own conclusion.\" and the offending direction removed\n   123\t  from the criteria. Each corrected pair's answer replaces its original; a new direction goes through stage 2; the whole set is\n   124\t  checked again. The rejected direction and its path are recorded. A circle that remains fails the article at `matched` (\"persistent\n   125\t  cycle\"), resumable, as PRD 06 says.\n   126\t- **Labels (code, §5)** are computed from the rungs as stored, inside the write, after C exists.\n   127\t- **Writer:** a link C reads T is written in step 2 with C's other dependencies; a link T reads C after C is created. Each row: the\n   128\t  article's seq, `direction` = the label, `kind = 'reads'`; T, when it is the reader, is added to the article's `changed` set, so the\n   129\t  day's round judges it after C when T is eligible (open, evidence in force, D59); a new C without evidence in force stays unjudged\n   130\t  and T reads it as \"not judged yet\". The plan is re-checked inside the write transaction (the graph, T still open); a mismatch raises\n   131\t  `WriteConflict` as today (the article fails, resumable).\n   132\t- **Store:** `dependencies.kind` (text). `ensure_writable_columns` adds it with default `''`; every existing row reads `''`.\n   133\t- **Filing:** `store.direct_parents` skips `kind = 'reads'` (D694 (a)); rows with `''` narrow exactly as today. `research_context`\n   134\t  reads dependency rows through an explicit column list (today `select *`), so its output keeps its shape.\n   135\t\n   136\t## 5. The label\n   137\t\n   138\t- **Typed direction** of a ladder (`links.typed_direction`): each rung is the interval [lo, hi) of its typed bounds; only the first\n   139\t  and the last rung may leave one outer end open (None); every inner rung has both bounds with lo < hi; an interval with lo ≥ hi is\n   140\t  invalid. The ladder runs −1 (values fall) when for every adjacent pair the next rung's hi is not above this rung's lo (touching\n   141\t  allowed), +1 when for every adjacent pair the next rung's lo is not below this rung's hi; anything else, an open inner end, or a\n   142\t  missing bound is None. Prose is not read (unlike `matching.ladder_direction`).\n   143\t- **The favourable end** is the end whose stored label is Strongly bullish (position 1, or position 5 for a successor stored\n   144\t  reversed). **Asset reader R reading T:** R's favourable end is its high end when that end is where R's values are high. T's end favourable to R: `together` → T's high end if R's favourable end is high, else\n   145\t  T's low end; `opposite` → the reverse. Label `first_is_bullish` when that end is T's first rung (T's high end is its first rung when\n   146\t  T's direction is −1), else `last_is_bullish`.\n   147\t- Worked case (old-2 07-10): R = v9 (direction −1, Strongly bullish first: favourable end high), T = v14 (−1), `together` → T's high\n   148\t  end = its first rung → `first_is_bullish`. Changing only the sign, only R's direction (its favourable end kept first), or only T's\n   149\t  direction each gives `last_is_bullish`; R stored reversed with its labels (favourable end last, direction +1) keeps the favourable\n   150\t  end high and gives `first_is_bullish`.\n   151\t- Eligibility (§1) already requires both directions decided, so a label is always defined for an asked pair.\n   152\t\n   153\t## 6. Table 1: state × event (C new in this article, T open and shown)\n   154\t\n   155\t\"Resumable\" below is the product path's behaviour; for poc-v119, whose only entry point is the July harness, a stopped sequence is final\n   156\t(§0).\n   157\t\n   158\t| Event | Outcome |\n   159\t|---|---|\n   160\t| matching settles C as `new`/`succession`; the pair is eligible; READS and SIGN pass | link proposed; graph check; written in C's commit; reader judged in that day's round after the read question, if eligible (D59) |\n   161\t| READS `neither` / below 0.5; SIGN `no_clear_sign` / below 0.5 | no link; recorded |\n   162\t| C merges into an existing question, is skipped or not opened, or coalesces with another candidate | not asked, or asked once for the canonical candidate |\n   163\t| a pair not eligible (theme, event, two-rung, untyped or shuffled bounds, same article) | not asked (D695) |\n   164\t| a proposed link closes a circle (with stored links, or among the article's own proposals) | one correction request per link on it; a remaining circle fails the article at `matched`, resumable |\n   165\t| the store holds an unbound waiting row | the link step refuses: the article fails at `matched` with that reason |\n   166\t| `jev.ask` fails (transport, answer shape) | the article fails at `matched`, resumable; a resume re-asks what the archive lacks |\n   167\t| the plan no longer fits at write time (T closed in between, a circle) | `WriteConflict`; the article fails, resumable |\n   168\t| a crash after selection and before the write | resume re-runs matching and selection from the archive (no new send) and writes once |\n   169\t| a crash after the write | the link is in the article's commit; a resumed day's round rebuilds its queue (`queued_by_ledger`) |\n   170\t| T's conclusion changes in a round | its reader queued once, after it (`queued_by_change`) |\n   171\t| T's comparison point changes with `changed=true` | the reader is queued in the same round and sees it |\n   172\t| T's comparison point changes with `changed=false` | the reader sees it at its next judgement (§3) |\n   173\t| T closes | the reader keeps reading T's closing conclusion marked \"closed\" (PRD 06's numeric branch) |\n   174\t| the reader closes | not judged; the row stays as history |\n   175\t| a later article shows C and T again | not asked: neither is new (two open questions are a later version) |\n   176\t| an awaited (waiting) row in the store | this version writes none; the admission rule above refuses a store holding one |\n   177\t| a second process writing the same store | refused: the harness holds `live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the run, and v119 has no other entry point (§0) |\n   178\t| a process dies after a provider attempt and before its answer reaches the archive | a death before settlement leaves the reservation counted against the ceiling (`SharedLedger.reserve`); a death after settlement leaves the settled charge counted; the sequence is stopped and final (§0), so no retry is free |\n   179\t| a version switch between completed days | allowed: the store's links and kinds are read the same by either version (§0); the July test switches from poc-v118 to poc-v119 at 07-10 |\n   180\t| a restart midway through a day (any configuration or input) | refused for v119: the harness refuses a store whose last day is unfinished and never resumes a stopped sequence (§0) |\n   181\t| a v118 run on a v119 store | §0 |\n   182\t\n   183\t## 7. Table 2: value × reader\n   184\t\n   185\t| Value | Readers |\n   186\t|---|---|\n   187\t| `dependencies` row with `kind='reads'` | judging: `topological`, `upstream`, `build_prompt`, `check_answer`, `queued_by_change`, `queued_by_ledger`; `store.would_cycle`, `dependants_of`, `dependencies_of`; `links.check_graph`; the service (`dependencies`, `dependants`), `bundle`, `search` records, `research_context` (explicit columns), the idea route: all read \"R depends on T\". `store.direct_parents` (filing) skips it. |\n   188\t| `kind=''` | every reader as today |\n   189\t| the `link_selections` row | the July test's readers and its shape test; no product reader, not preflight, not the trace |\n   190\t| T added to `changed` | `round.changed_views_of_day` → `judge_day` |\n   191\t| `current_state.reference`, `.implied_outcome` | the judging-v8 block only |\n   192\t\n   193\t## 8. Table 3: new path × old checks\n   194\t\n   195\t| Check | Under poc-v119 |\n   196\t|---|---|\n   197\t| no-link requests byte-equal | proved at $0: poc-v119 over old-2's 07-01..07-09 with the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport equals the rebuilt v118 prefix (every other request from the archive) |\n   198\t| filing under seed-style rows | unchanged (`kind ''`); the existing test stays green |\n   199\t| filing with a `reads` row | no link removed: re-file old-2's stored readings after seq 148 with the link present (105 shared statements, `filing-exposure.md`) |\n   200\t| `cites_views` only names shown dependencies | unchanged |\n   201\t| dependencies judged first | unchanged |\n   202\t| `matching.check` refusals fail the article | selection runs after it and never adds to its refusals |\n   203\t| preflight and the trace (read `match_records` by `call_no`) | untouched: the selection is in `link_selections` |\n   204\t| D59, the theme block | unchanged |\n   205\t| frozen-piece pins | §0 |\n   206\t\n   207\t## 9. Table 4: prior decisions\n   208\t\n   209\tD51, D368 item 2 (the matching step chooses: a Jev question); D191 point 2 (an existing question gains a link when the read question\n   210\topens); D695 (number questions only, one new); D207, D265, D694 (a) (a link moves no statement); D260 (the reader sees the comparison\n   211\tpoint and the forecast); D248 (same quantity and period is one question); PRD 06 (cycles corrected, then normal failure); D354, D359\n   212\t(new versions); D542's five items: a circle through a waiting link cannot arise (no waiting link is written), closing as table 1,\n   213\ttheme twice and historical readers not reached (no theme link, no resolution row), `last_end` absent; the unbound-wait admission\n   214\trule (§4) as the guard for a waiting circle.\n   215\t\n   216\t## 10. Round-4 findings and where they are answered\n   217\t\n   218\tRound 7: 1 ordinary writers refuse a harness ledger: §0. 2 the serial item runner, sequence-bound authorization and post-commit\n   219\tinspection: `TEST-PLAN.md`. Nonblocking: a Jev failure before any proposal writes `failed` alone (§1 step 6, §11 test 2); crash\n   220\taccounting wording (§6); \"resumable\" rows read with §0 for v119.\n   221\tRound 6: 1 writer and restart boundary: §0, §6. 2 durable selection and failure record: §1 step 6. 3 the July allow-list before\n   222\tthe budget transport, the out-of-pair stop at inspection: `TEST-PLAN.md`. Nonblocking: examples (§2), effective targets (§4), the\n   223\tadmission rule in Table 4 (§9), tests 2, 3 (§11).\n   224\tRound 5: 1 sign batching: §1 step 4, §2. 2 the whole graph and waits: §4. 3 archive: `TEST-PLAN.md`. 4 placement, interface, record:\n   225\t§1 steps 6–7. 5 reversed successors, event measures, intervals: §1 step 2, §5. 6 July dry run, extra links, budget: `TEST-PLAN.md`.\n   226\t7 restart and judging rows: §6. Renderer continuation lines: §3.\n   227\tRound 4: 1 final identity: §1 steps 1–2. 2 one graph, refusals recorded, PRD 06 correction: §1 step 6, §4. 3 lifecycle and theme boundary:\n   228\tD695, §6. 4 July harness: `TEST-PLAN.md` (archive, sequences, dry run, unexpected links, budget). 5 question texts: §2. 6 typed\n   229\tladders: §5. 7 failure and restart rows: §6. Compatibility (current_state, research_context, mixing, pins, entry points): §0, §3, §4.\n   230\t\n   231\t## 11. Tests (with the code; each names its row)\n   232\t\n   233\t1. `typed_direction` and the label: the worked case, its three mirrors, a reversed stored successor, a shuffled middle, touching and\n   234\t   overlapping bounds, an open inner end, prose-only bounds (None).\n   235\t2. Selection under `jev-links` with a fake Jev transport: eligibility (theme, two-rung, same-article and merge cases not asked);\n   236\t   stage 1 and 2 decisions; one sign job holding both reading directions; the canonical candidate asked once; under `jev` no question\n   237\t   asked (mutant: asked); `link_selections` rows `proposed` then `committed`; `proposed` then `failed` on a write conflict; `failed`\n   238\t   alone, with the partial answers and the failing request's sha, on a Jev error before any proposal.\n   239\t3. Graph and correction: a circle with a stored path corrected; the four-link circle through two openings found and corrected; a\n   240\t   persistent circle fails the article; a store with an unbound waiting row refused; a bound legacy wait passes the admission rule and\n   241\t   takes part in the circle check through its bound target; no circle written.\n   242\t4. Writer: T reads C written with `kind='reads'`, T in `changed`; WriteConflict when T closed.\n   243\t5. Filing: `direct_parents` skips `reads` (mutant: it narrows); seed-style rows narrow (existing test).\n   244\t6. judging-v8 block exact text, with a multi-line comparison point, forecast and reasons; v7 block byte-equal to today's; no-link\n   245\t   request byte-equal under v7 and v8; a comparison-point change with `changed=true` queues the reader, with `changed=false` does not.\n   246\t8. `link_selections` shape pinned; `writing.write`'s existing six-argument callers (`tests/test_identity_repair.py`) unchanged.\n   247\t7. Entry points: `config.load` accepts `jev-links`; `round._match` and the parallel day treat it as Jev; `scripts/replay.py` and\n   248\t   `budget_replay.py` refuse it (mutant: they accept it); the v118 CLI pointed at an unfinished harness-only ledger refuses before\n   249\t   routing any item (mutant: it routes).\n     1\t# The July test: harness, archive, budget and reading rule (D694 (c); for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\t## Starting state ($0, done)\n     4\t`rebuild_control.py` → `rebuild-control.log`: old-2 replayed under poc-v118 from 07-01 to 07-09 with a transport that refuses every\n     5\tsend (`only_objects={'NVDA'}`, the comparison launcher's default): 160 items, 55 judgements, all from the archive; equal to old-2's\n     6\tfinished store up to seq 147 on views, keys, rungs, evidence, links, judgements (rung, reasons, cites, changed, reference, implied\n     7\toutcome, request sha), view switches, successions and dependencies. Each sequence starts from its own copy of this ledger.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Before any send ($0, to be built and run)\n    10\t1. **Prefix compatibility:** poc-v119 over 07-01..07-09 from empty, the link questions answered by a fixed `neither` transport, every\n    11\t   other request from the archive: the ledger equals the rebuilt prefix. This proves only that v119 with no link reproduces the\n    12\t   prefix; what a live v119 would have selected before 07-10 is not counted, and the linked arm starts from the v118 prefix by design\n    13\t   (the July test accepts the existing-reader / new-target case only, D694 (b)). The eligible pairs v119 would have asked before\n    14\t   07-10 are listed from the run's `link_selections` so the reader can see them.\n    15\t2. **The archive, proved:** each sequence's archive is a writable copy of old-2's archive (call ids kept) in which every stored judge\n    16\t   row for v9 or v14 (request user text beginning \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\") is retired by the existing `Archive.retire`\n    17\t   (its request sha gains a suffix), so no exact lookup can return it. At $0 with a recording fake transport: an exact old v9 request\n    18\t   goes to the transport; an exact old request of another question is answered from the archive; an answer the check refuses is\n    19\t   retired and is not returned again.\n    20\t3. **Dry run:** the whole harness for 07-10..07-12 with a fixed fake transport for every call that would be bought: two control and\n    21\t   two linked dry sequences whose 07-10 answers for v9 and v14 differ (labelled \"DRY-A\", \"DRY-B\"). Every request that runs after the\n    22\t   first must carry its own sequence's last accepted answer. The control must judge v9 only on the days the stored run did (no v9\n    23\t   judgement on 07-11). The linked dry sequences must write \"v9 reads v14\" at seq 148 (fixed Jev answers) and show the judging-v8 block\n    24\t   in v9's requests; one with v14 `changed=true` on 07-11 must queue v9 that day, one with `changed=false` must not. Every other\n    25\t   request must be answered from the archive. Both stop paths are exercised with the recording fake: an unapproved request (a third\n    26\t   question's judge call) is refused before any reservation; an otherwise valid link request at another sequence than 148 is refused\n    27\t   before any reservation; a committed out-of-pair link whose reader would never be judged stops the sequence at inspection, before a\n    28\t   further reservation.\n    29\t4. **The rebuilt requests priced** at published rates (`model.PRICES`) to set the reservation; the reading rule frozen.\n    30\t\n    31\t## The sequences\n    32\tThree linked (poc-v119) and three control (poc-v118), each: its own copy of the prefix ledger, marked harness-only (DESIGN §0);\n    33\t`only_objects={'NVDA'}`; 07-10 to 07-12; `replay.run` with the harness's **serial item runner** as its `day_runner`: for each routed\n    34\titem, in order, it calls `round.run` with a transport bound to that item's own sequence number, then yields the result; the day's\n    35\tjudging gets the judging-scope transport through `replay.run`'s `transport`.\n    36\t\n    37\t**Archive per sequence:** its own writable copy of old-2's archive with the v9 and v14 judge rows retired (step 2 above), so both\n    38\tquestions are judged fresh every day (council R round 3) and every other request replays by exact identity. The harness holds\n    39\t`live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the run, refuses a store whose last day is unfinished, and never resumes a stopped\n    40\tsequence (DESIGN §0).\n    41\t\n    42\t**The allow-list, in front of the budget transport:** every request that misses the archive reaches a wrapper before the budget\n    43\ttransport. The judging-scope wrapper passes only a judge request whose user text begins \"Thesis v9 (\" or \"Thesis v14 (\"; the item-scope\n    44\twrapper, built by the serial item runner for one item, passes only Jev requests whose questions are all link questions (the READS and\n    45\tSIGN builders' keys), and only when that item's sequence is 148, in the linked arm. Anything else raises before any reservation, which\n    46\tstops the sequence. The wrapper counts, per target judgement, the provider attempts; the harness asserts\n    47\tthat every v9 and v14 judgement of 07-10..07-12 was answered by a provider attempt of its own sequence (fresh), never by the archive.\n    48\t\n    49\t**The out-of-pair stop at inspection:** when `round.run` returns successfully for seq 148, the serial item runner reads the store's\n    50\t`dependencies` rows with `kind='reads'` before it starts the next item or yields to the day's judging: any row whose reader is not v9\n    51\tor v14 stops the sequence there (not comparable), whether or not that reader would ever be judged.\n    52\t\n    53\t**Transport:** the shared reservation ledger of the comparison runs (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py`\n    54\t`SharedLedger`, `BudgetTransport`, with `install_stop_gate`), one ceiling of **$0.15** for all six sequences, used as it behaves: a\n    55\tLuna call reserves its worst case per attempt and settles at its reported usage; a Jev call reserves its whole internal retry bundle\n    56\tand settles at up to the attempts times the reported usage, or at the reservation when usage is unavailable. After a sequence stops,\n    57\tthe shared ledger is read: a refused reservation makes the comparison **inconclusive**, even where `round.run` reports it as a matching\n    58\tor judging failure; an overrun or an unknown charge is reported from the ledger.\n    59\t\n    60\t**Expected new requests:** the v9 and v14 judge calls, the link questions of the item at seq 148 (linked arm), and a v9 judge call\n    61\ton any day it is queued by a changed v14. **Any other archive miss** (extraction, matching, another question's judgement) stops that\n    62\tsequence and is reported. Registered now for extra links the real selection may write besides \"v9 reads v14\" (for example with the\n    63\tstand-alone CPU question v8): the selection is kept and reported; a link whose reader is v9 or v14 changes a scored request and the\n    64\tsequence is scored as it ran, with the extra link named in the report; a link whose reader is any other question stops the sequence\n    65\tat inspection (above), and the sequence counts as not comparable. A missing \"v9\n    66\treads v14\", or v14 reading v9, is a selection miss.\n    67\t\n    68\t## Reading rule (frozen before the send; council R round 2, `codex-r2.md` §7(b), with round 3)\n    69\t- **A. Comparable answers:** both 07-12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity (a range by its stated ends);\n    70\t  quarters recorded where both give comparable figures; a missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested.\n    71\t- **B. Arithmetic and sources:** reported figures keep their amount and scope; the arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within\n    72\t  rounding; each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day; a linked\n    73\t  forecast is treated as a forecast with assumptions.\n    74\t- **C. Room for the rest:** the high end of the Data Center forecast is at least $6B below the low end of the company forecast (the Q1\n    75\t  floor: $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center); each comparable quarter keeps the segment within the total.\n    76\t- **D. The link did the work (linked arm):** matching chose \"v9 reads v14\", the writer committed it at seq 148, and v9 used v14's\n    77\t  forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound; delivery and use of the Bloomberg-compiled $393B (e195) recorded separately; a\n    78\t  mention or citation alone earns no credit.\n    79\t- **Pass:** at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D; at most one control meets A–C; no first-attempt refusal added and no new\n    80\t  material grounding error on either question across 07-10..07-12 (relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating\n    81\t  $393B as a Data Center consensus, is one). **Inconclusive:** two or more controls reconcile, fewer than two comparable sequences in\n    82\t  either arm, or a ceiling stop. **Fail:** a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other\n    83\t  miss. Failures take precedence.\n    84\t- **Readers:** Claude's marks written first, then a fresh blind Codex reader on the six sequences under shuffled labels, the key outside\n    85\t  the repository; every sequence reported.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '18,149p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;128,166p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '82,112p'\nnl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '25,96p'\nnl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '262,311p;337,371p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/replay.py | sed -n '18,149p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/round.py | sed -n '27,61p;128,166p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '82,112p'\nnl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '25,96p'\nnl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '262,311p;337,371p'\"","aggregated_output":"    18\t    \"\"\"A saved parallel extraction cannot establish that it read its predecessors.\"\"\"\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\tdef refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn):\n    22\t    \"\"\"D159: preserve old handovers, but never resume a day-start read as a sequential read.\"\"\"\n    23\t    pending = conn.execute(\"\"\"select p.input_id, p.reason from processing_steps p\n    24\t        where p.step='extracted' and p.result='ok'\n    25\t        and p.id=(select max(q.id) from processing_steps q\n    26\t                  where q.input_id=p.input_id and q.step='extracted' and q.result='ok')\n    27\t        and not exists (select 1 from processing_steps q\n    28\t                        where q.input_id=p.input_id and q.step='handed_over' and q.result='ok')\n    29\t        order by p.sequence_no\"\"\")\n    30\t    ids = [row['input_id'] for row in pending if row['reason'].endswith(' (parallel)')]\n    31\t    if ids:\n    32\t        raise StaleHandoverError('unfinished day-start extractions; keep this ledger and replay into a new one: ' + ', '.join(ids))\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tclass LookAheadError(RuntimeError):\n    36\t    pass\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tclass BackdatingError(RuntimeError):\n    40\t    pass\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef calendar_days(from_day, until_day):\n    44\t    day = datetime.date.fromisoformat(from_day)\n    45\t    last = datetime.date.fromisoformat(until_day)\n    46\t    while day <= last:\n    47\t        yield day.isoformat()\n    48\t        day += datetime.timedelta(days=1)\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef run(*, testdb_path, views_path, archive, cfg, universe, from_day, until_day, day0=None, spend_cap_usd=None,\n    52\t        transport=None, log=print, only_objects=None, max_items_per_day=None, day_runner=None):\n    53\t    items_db = testdb.open_db(testdb_path)\n    54\t    conn = store.open_db(views_path)\n    55\t    refuse_unfinished_parallel(conn)\n    56\t    last_done = store.last_completed_day(conn)\n    57\t    start = from_day\n    58\t    if last_done and from_day <= last_done:\n    59\t        next_day = (datetime.date.fromisoformat(last_done) + datetime.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()\n    60\t        if next_day > until_day:\n    61\t            raise BackdatingError(f'views database already completed {last_done}; nothing to run before it')\n    62\t        log(f'resuming after the last completed day {last_done}')\n    63\t        start = next_day\n    64\t    last_written = conn.execute('select max(publication_day) from processing_steps where sequence_no > 0').fetchone()[0]\n    65\t    if last_written and start < last_written:\n    66\t        raise BackdatingError(f'views database already holds rounds of {last_written}; a replay cannot start before it (D31)')\n    67\t    totals = {'items': 0, 'extracted': 0, 'skipped': 0, 'merged': 0, 'not_processed': 0, 'returned': 0, 'failed': 0,\n    68\t              'evidence': 0, 'new_views': 0, 'judged': 0, 'changed': 0, 'closed': 0}\n    69\t    calls_before, cost_before, *_ = archive.totals()\n    70\t    for day in calendar_days(start, until_day):\n    71\t        day_stats = {k: 0 for k in totals}\n    72\t        day_cost_before = archive.totals()[1]\n    73\t        processed = 0\n    74\t        to_run = []\n    75\t        for item in testdb.feed(items_db, day, day):\n    76\t            if item['publication_day'] > day:\n    77\t                raise LookAheadError(f'{item[\"input_id\"]} is dated {item[\"publication_day\"]}, after replay day {day}')\n    78\t            if only_objects and not any(o['value'] in only_objects for o in item['object_identifiers']):\n    79\t                continue\n    80\t            if max_items_per_day and processed >= max_items_per_day:\n    81\t                break\n    82\t            day_stats['items'] += 1\n    83\t            route = dispatch.route(conn, item, universe)\n    84\t            if route.kind != 'extract':\n    85\t                day_stats[route.kind] += 1\n    86\t                if route.kind == 'skipped':\n    87\t                    processed += 1      # written by an earlier run of this day: a restart keeps the day's item limit\n    88\t                if route.kind == 'merged':\n    89\t                    dispatch.mark(conn, item, 0, 'merged', 'ok', route.reason)\n    90\t                    conn.commit()\n    91\t                continue\n    92\t            processed += 1\n    93\t            to_run.append((item, route))\n    94\t        results = (day_runner(conn, archive, cfg, universe, to_run, day=day, transport=transport, log=log) if day_runner else\n    95\t                   (round_module.run(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, route.sequence_no, resume_from=route.resume_from, transport=transport, log=log)\n    96\t                    for item, route in to_run))\n    97\t        finished = 0\n    98\t        try:\n    99\t            for index, result in enumerate(results):\n   100\t                if index >= len(to_run) or result.input_id != to_run[index][0]['input_id']:\n   101\t                    raise RuntimeError('day runner returned results out of input order')\n   102\t                finished += 1\n   103\t                day_stats['extracted'] += 1\n   104\t                day_stats['evidence'] += result.evidence\n   105\t                day_stats['new_views'] += result.new_views\n   106\t                day_stats['judged'] += result.judged\n   107\t                day_stats['changed'] += result.changed\n   108\t                if result.failed:\n   109\t                    day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   110\t                    log(f'  ! {result.input_id[:60]}: {result.failed}')\n   111\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'item failed; day {day} remains resumable: {result.failed}')\n   112\t                if spend_cap_usd is not None and archive.totals()[1] - cost_before > spend_cap_usd:\n   113\t                    raise RuntimeError(f'spend cap {spend_cap_usd} reached on {day}')\n   114\t        finally:\n   115\t            if hasattr(results, 'close'):\n   116\t                results.close()\n   117\t        if finished != len(to_run):\n   118\t            raise RuntimeError('day runner did not complete every routed item')\n   119\t        seq = store.next_sequence(conn) - 1\n   120\t        judged = round_module.judge_day(conn, archive, cfg, day, seq, transport=transport, log=log)\n   121\t        day_stats['judged'] += judged.judged\n   122\t        day_stats['changed'] += judged.changed\n   123\t        if judged.failed:\n   124\t            day_stats['failed'] += 1\n   125\t            log(f'  ! day judging: {judged.failed}')\n   126\t            raise RuntimeError(f'judging failed; day {day} remains resumable: {judged.failed}')\n   127\t        closed = pull.end_of_day(conn, day, seq)\n   128\t        day_stats['closed'] = len(closed)\n   129\t        # The day ends at the last sequence it wrote, a closing's own sequence on a day without items included, so the next day starts after it.\n   130\t        store.complete_day(conn, day, store.next_sequence(conn) - 1, time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   131\t        conn.commit()\n   132\t        for key in totals:\n   133\t            totals[key] += day_stats[key]\n   134\t        calls, cost, _, _ = archive.totals()\n   135\t        day_cost = cost - day_cost_before  # Includes discarded speculative calls and repaired refusals.\n   136\t        open_count = len(store.open_views(conn))\n   137\t        log(f'{day} | items {day_stats[\"items\"]:3d} extracted {day_stats[\"extracted\"]:3d} merged {day_stats[\"merged\"]:2d} skipped {day_stats[\"not_processed\"]:2d} '\n   138\t            f'failed {day_stats[\"failed\"]:2d} | evidence {day_stats[\"evidence\"]:3d} new views {day_stats[\"new_views\"]:2d} judged {day_stats[\"judged\"]:3d} '\n   139\t            f'changed {day_stats[\"changed\"]:3d} closed {len(closed)} | open views {open_count} | day ${day_cost:.2f} total ${cost - cost_before:.2f} calls {calls - calls_before}')\n   140\t        if day0 and day == day0:\n   141\t            conn.commit()\n   142\t            shutil.copy(views_path, views_path + '.day0.sqlite')\n   143\t            log(f'day 0 snapshot written: {views_path}.day0.sqlite')\n   144\t    return totals\n    27\tdef _fail(conn, item, seq, result, step, kind, detail, pool_key):\n    28\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, step, 'failed', detail[:300])\n    29\t    store.pool(conn, kind, pool_key, {'input_id': item['input_id'], 'error': detail[:300]}, seq)\n    30\t    result.failed = detail[:200]\n    31\t    conn.commit()\n    32\t    return result\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, *, extra_views=(), call_offset=0, transport=None, workers=1):\n    36\t    \"\"\"One matching call with one retry on a refused check. Returns Checked, or None after marking the failure.\"\"\"\n    37\t    note = ''\n    38\t    checked = None\n    39\t    engine = jev_matching if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else matching      # Jev answers once; a retry would be the same answer\n    40\t    for attempt in range(1 if engine is jev_matching else 2):\n    41\t        try:\n    42\t            options = {'workers': workers, 'llm_transport': transport} if engine is jev_matching else {}     # the collision judge sends with the caller's transport too\n    43\t            answer = engine.decide(archive, cfg, conn, item, candidates, evidence, lists, shown, extra_views=extra_views, retry_note=note, transport=transport, **options)\n    44\t        except Exception as error:\n    45\t            _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_failed', 'matching: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n    46\t            return None\n    47\t        result.cost += answer.cost_usd\n    48\t        result.cached_calls += int(answer.cached)\n    49\t        checked = matching.check(conn, universe, answer.data, candidates, evidence, lists, shown)\n    50\t        shown_record = {'candidates': lists.candidate_lists, 'evidence': {f'{k[0]}|{k[1]}': v for k, v in lists.evidence_lists.items()}}\n    51\t        if getattr(answer, 'request_records', None):\n    52\t            shown_record['requests'] = answer.request_records\n    53\t        store.insert(conn, 'match_records', seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], call_no=call_offset + attempt + 1,\n    54\t                     shown_json=json.dumps(shown_record),\n    55\t                     request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, call_id=answer.call_id, decisions_json=json.dumps(answer.data, ensure_ascii=False),\n    56\t                     checks_json=json.dumps({'refusals': checked.refusals, 'not_opened': checked.not_opened, 'notes': checked.notes}, ensure_ascii=False), written_json=None)\n    57\t        if not checked.refusals:\n    58\t            return checked\n    59\t        note = '；'.join(checked.refusals)\n    60\t    _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'matched', 'matching_refused_twice', 'matching refused twice: ' + note, item['category'])\n    61\t    return None\n   128\t    # first matching call: the candidates and the evidence linked straight to existing views\n   129\t    lists = matching.build_lists(conn, handover, shown, cfg.search_top_n)\n   130\t    checked = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, handover.candidates, handover.evidence, lists, shown, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   131\t    if checked is None:\n   132\t        return result\n   133\t    # second call: evidence linked to candidates that attached to an existing view, compared under that view\n   134\t    second_pass = {}\n   135\t    pending = []\n   136\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   137\t        for link in e['links']:\n   138\t            outcome = checked.outcomes.get(link)\n   139\t            if outcome and outcome[0] == 'merge':\n   140\t                pending.append((e, outcome[1]))\n   141\t    if pending:\n   142\t        lists2 = matching.Lists({}, {(e['id'], view_id): matching.rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], cfg.search_top_n) for e, view_id in pending})\n   143\t        evidence2, seen = [], set()\n   144\t        for e, view_id in pending:\n   145\t            if e['id'] not in seen:\n   146\t                evidence2.append(dict(e, links=[v for x, v in pending if x['id'] == e['id']]))\n   147\t                seen.add(e['id'])\n   148\t        checked2 = _match(conn, archive, cfg, universe, item, seq, result, [], evidence2, lists2, [], extra_views=sorted({v for _, v in pending}),\n   149\t                          call_offset=2, transport=transport, workers=matching_workers)\n   150\t        if checked2 is None:\n   151\t            return result\n   152\t        second_pass = checked2.evidence\n   153\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'matched', 'ok', f'{len(checked.outcomes)} candidates placed')\n   154\t    # write, and record what changed in the same commit (a resume at 'judged' reads it)\n   155\t    try:\n   156\t        written = writing.write(conn, universe, seq, item, handover, checked, second_pass)\n   157\t    except Exception as error:\n   158\t        return _fail(conn, item, seq, result, 'written', 'writing_failed', 'writing: ' + repr(error), type(error).__name__)\n   159\t    result.new_views = len(set(written.new_views.values()))\n   160\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'written', 'ok', json.dumps({'changed': sorted(written.changed_views), 'new': written.new_views, 'notes': written.notes[:20]}, ensure_ascii=False))\n   161\t    dispatch.mark(conn, item, seq, 'handed_over', 'ok', '')\n   162\t    conn.commit()\n   163\t    return result\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   106\t                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   107\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(answers, ensure_ascii=False) if answers is not None else None,\n   108\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   109\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   110\t    if problems:\n   111\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(problems[:5]))\n   112\t    return model.Answer(answers, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n    25\t\n    26\tfrom hivemind import config, model, parallel_day, replay, universe  # noqa: E402\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\tdef refuse_seeded_ledger(path):\n    30\t    \"\"\"A new run cannot reuse questions inserted by the retired seeding path.\"\"\"\n    31\t    ledger = Path(path)\n    32\t    if not ledger.exists():\n    33\t        return\n    34\t    try:\n    35\t        with sqlite3.connect(ledger.resolve().as_uri() + '?mode=ro', uri=True) as conn:\n    36\t            tables = {r[0] for r in conn.execute(\"select name from sqlite_master where type='table'\")}\n    37\t            if not tables:\n    38\t                return\n    39\t            if 'views' not in tables:\n    40\t                raise SystemExit('cannot verify question origins in the existing ledger')\n    41\t            columns = {r[1] for r in conn.execute('pragma table_info(views)')}\n    42\t            if 'created_from_input' not in columns:\n    43\t                raise SystemExit('cannot verify question origins in the existing ledger')\n    44\t            seeded = conn.execute(\"select count(*) from views where lower(substr(created_from_input, 1, 5))='seed:'\").fetchone()[0]\n    45\t            if seeded:\n    46\t                raise SystemExit(f'existing ledger has {seeded} seeded questions; use a clean ledger')\n    47\t    except sqlite3.Error as error:\n    48\t        raise SystemExit(f'cannot inspect existing ledger: {error}') from error\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef main():\n    52\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    53\t    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day', required=True)\n    54\t    parser.add_argument('--until', dest='until_day', required=True)\n    55\t    parser.add_argument('--day0', default=None)\n    56\t    parser.add_argument('--testdb', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    57\t    parser.add_argument('--views', required=True, help='the ledger this run writes (a new run: a new dated folder)')\n    58\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', required=True, help='the model-call archive of this run')\n    59\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118.json'))\n    60\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    61\t    parser.add_argument('--only', default=None, help='comma-separated object ids to restrict the stream to')\n    62\t    parser.add_argument('--cap', type=float, default=None, help='USD spend cap for this run')\n    63\t    parser.add_argument('--max-items-per-day', type=int, default=None)\n    64\t    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=16, help='extraction requests prepared at a time (D183); 1 is the serial path')\n    65\t    parser.add_argument('--jev-workers', type=int, default=None,\n    66\t                        help='Jev matching questions sent at a time when --workers > 1; default 8 for Jev, 1 for another engine')\n    67\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n    68\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n    69\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n    70\t\n    71\t    def log(*parts):\n    72\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n    73\t        print(line, flush=True)\n    74\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    75\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n    76\t\n    77\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n    78\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n    79\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses retired seeded-question baseline; select a configuration without it')\n    80\t    refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n    81\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n    82\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n    83\t    day_runner = None\n    84\t    if args.workers > 1:\n    85\t        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n    86\t        day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n    87\t                                              extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers)\n    88\t    log(f'--- replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version}'\n    89\t        f' workers {args.workers}')\n    90\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n    91\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, day0=args.day0, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n    92\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, max_items_per_day=args.max_items_per_day,\n    93\t                        day_runner=day_runner)\n    94\t    log('totals:', totals)\n    95\t\n    96\t\n   262\tclass BudgetTransport:\n   263\t    \"\"\"Called as production calls a transport: (provider, request) for a language model, (request,) for Jev.\"\"\"\n   264\t\n   265\t    def __init__(self, ledger, sleep=time.sleep):\n   266\t        self.ledger, self.sleep = ledger, sleep\n   267\t\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   292\t\n   293\t    def _jev(self, request):\n   294\t        estimate = jev_estimate(request)\n   295\t        if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   296\t            raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   297\t        try:\n   298\t            response = jev.transport(request)\n   299\t        except Exception:\n   300\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate, kind='jev')\n   301\t            raise\n   302\t        usage = response.get('usage') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   303\t        tokens = usage.get('input_tokens') if isinstance(usage, dict) else None\n   304\t        if isinstance(tokens, int) and not isinstance(tokens, bool) and tokens > 0:\n   305\t            # an unanswered attempt inside jev.transport was the same request, so each of the three is billed at most this input;\n   306\t            # the whole charge is settled, so a charge above the reservation sets the overrun flag\n   307\t            actual = jev.ATTEMPTS * tokens * model.PRICES[request['model']][0] / 1e6\n   308\t        else:\n   309\t            actual = estimate                       # usage missing, invalid, or zero for a nonempty request: the whole reservation\n   310\t        self.ledger.settle(estimate, actual, kind='jev', tokens=tokens if isinstance(tokens, int) else None)\n   311\t        return response\n   337\t    for name in ('ledger', 'from_day', 'until_day', 'views', 'archive'):\n   338\t        if not getattr(args, name):\n   339\t            raise SystemExit(f'--{name.replace(\"_day\", \"\")} is required')\n   340\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n   341\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n   342\t\n   343\t    def log(*parts):\n   344\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n   345\t        print(line, flush=True)\n   346\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   347\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n   348\t\n   349\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n   350\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n   351\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses the retired seeded-question baseline: refused')\n   352\t    import importlib.util\n   353\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('scripts_replay', ROOT / 'scripts/replay.py')\n   354\t    scripts_replay = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n   355\t    spec.loader.exec_module(scripts_replay)\n   356\t    scripts_replay.refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)          # the same refusal scripts/replay.py makes\n   357\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   358\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n   359\t    ledger = SharedLedger(args.ledger)\n   360\t    install_stop_gate(ledger)                              # Jev's internal retries read the run's stop too (council mo R1)\n   361\t    transport = BudgetTransport(ledger)\n   362\t    jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n   363\t    day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n   364\t                                          extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers) if args.workers > 1 else None\n   365\t    log(f'--- budgeted replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version} '\n   366\t        f'workers {args.workers}; ledger {args.ledger} {ledger.read()}')\n   367\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n   368\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n   369\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, transport=transport, day_runner=day_runner)\n   370\t    log('totals:', totals)\n   371\t    log('ledger:', ledger.read())\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"**Version 5 closes both round-7 blockers.** The design is ready to implement and verify at $0. The July send still follows the council’s review of that proof. [D694](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10439)\n\n- **Harness ledger.** Both ordinary launchers already have a place to inspect the ledger before calling `replay.run`. Checking the `harness_only` marker there under every configuration closes the v118 write path identified in round 7. The harness lock handles a second harness process. [Design §0](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:9) · [Ordinary replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:77) · [Budgeted replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py:349)\n- **Serial runner and allow-list.** `replay.run` gives the runner each item’s routed sequence. The runner can bind that sequence into the transport it passes to `round.run`, so `jev.ask` can keep passing only the request. A successful `round.run` returns after the commit. That gives the runner the right point to inspect seq 148 and stop before the next item or judging. The day’s judging receives the separate transport passed to `replay.run`. Both wrappers can refuse a miss before the budget transport reserves anything. [July harness plan](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:31) · [Replay seam](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:94) · [Article commit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/round.py:153) · [Jev transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/jev.py:87)\n\n## Nonblocking\n\n- Reword §0’s remaining “v119 store opened by v118: allowed” sentence to mean read-only inspection and the v7 renderer compatibility test. The ordinary writers must refuse the marked ledger. [Design §0](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md:17)\n- Use an explicit stop reason for the post-commit inspection. Ending the runner early would otherwise produce replay’s generic “day runner did not complete every routed item” error. In the dry run, tie each fresh judgement to its own call record so a later archive hit cannot count as another fresh sample. [Replay completion check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/replay.py:114) · [Freshness assertion](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/TEST-PLAN.md:42)\n\n**READY TO BUILD.**"}}
{"type":"turn.completed","usage":{"input_tokens":13963314,"cached_input_tokens":13541248,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":54076,"reasoning_output_tokens":21982}}
